{
  "_": [
    "docs/design/FLOOR.md § 4.6 — THE ONE STATEMENT of how a layout, the installs the fleet reports and the rooms with an",
    "authored map compose into floors. Two runtimes implement it — App\\Building\\Building::compose() for the admin console",
    "and public/js/lobby/lobby-model.js floors() for the lobby and the floor route — and both are held to every case here",
    "(Tests\\Feature\\Building, Tests\\Feature\\Lobby). A case is the RAW authored document (a list of floor records, each",
    "carrying its `name`, optionally its `aliases` (card#13117), its `rooms` — a mapping of install id to that room's RECORD,",
    "`{\"form\": …}` and, on a planned floor, `{\"origin\": …}` (card#9292) — optionally its `theme` (card#11046) and its",
    "`hallway`), the installs the fleet reports, the rooms with an authored map (`authored`), and the floors that must come",
    "out: the named floors by key — the slug of the name — ascending, then the Unassigned floor (key `unassigned`, name",
    "`Unassigned`, no aliases, the house theme) when any room no floor places is reported or authored; each floor's `name`",
    "and `aliases`, rooms by install ascending, each room's `origin` where the floor is planned, and `reported` per room,",
    "and each floor's `theme` as the entry names it (null where it names none — card#11046).",
    "⚠ A floor's `hallway` is deliberately NOT among them: it is a whole Tiled document that only the floor SCREEN draws,",
    "and the cases pin both runtimes to leaving it in the layout.",
    "Add a case here and both suites gain it; a rule that lives in one runtime and not the other is what this file",
    "exists to red."
  ],
